{
  "description": "#6054 D3 — the edge into DONE makes a repeating task's next occurrence (`set_todo_state_in_tx` -> `build_recurrence_sibling_in_tx`), on both callers that write one state: `set_todo_state` and `set_property` with key `todo_state`. The occurrence is appended under the original's parent (`create_block`), then written in the backend's order: `todo_state` TODO, `repeat`, the shifted `due_date` and `scheduled_date`, `repeat-origin`; the digest pins that order. Every rule here is `+` mode, which shifts from the task's own date: `daily`, `weekly` across a year end on both dates, `monthly` from Jan 31 (clamped to Feb 28, and the clamp sticks on the next completion), and `+3d`. The `.+` and `++` modes shift from `chrono::Local::now()`, so no fixture can pin their dates; the mock's unit tests pin them with a fixed now. A DONE task completed again makes nothing, an undated task's occurrence has no dates, and an occurrence's own occurrence points `repeat-origin` at the first task of the chain. Payload-replayed ops do not run recurrence on the backend, so every DONE here rides `via: \"command\"`. Seed: S1 (Chores) > S2 (daily), S3 (weekly), S4 (monthly), S5 (+3d), S6 > [S7 (daily, undated), S8]. Re-author `expected` / `expected_ops` / `expected_queries` via CONFORMANCE_UPDATE=1.",
